Actually, I realize `\ContinuedFloat` maintains the figure counter, but the caption handling gets complicated. A simpler approach would be to either use separate figures with the main caption only on the last one and minimal labels on each, or skip captions on intermediate panels entirely and just show the figure content.

The cleanest solution with `\ContinuedFloat` is to place the full caption only on the final panel while letting the earlier panels display without captions, keeping them all under the same figure counter. I'm settling on a cleaner split: three panels in the first figure and two in the second, which should each fit comfortably on a page with surrounding text given their individual heights.

Since each panel generates separately, I'll use individual `\begin{figure}[t]` blocks with `\ContinuedFloat` for panels after the first, placing the full caption only on the last panel to avoid counter issues.

